From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sensapi, connect: IsDestinationReachable and IsInternetConnected check the routing table (3741)

sensapi, connect: IsDestinationReachable and IsInternetConnected check the routing table

IsDestinationReachable resolves the destination and asks for the interface
the routing table would use; the link speed of that interface goes to the QOC
info. IsInternetConnected is S_OK when a public address has a route and S_FALSE
otherwise. Both always said yes.

Rebased at integration (integ-2026-10) onto 3292 (fast-a): sensapi was implemented twice (section 9 named it); fast-a 3292's IsNetworkAlive/IsDestinationReachable kept, 3741's dlls/sensapi hunks dropped; 3741 keeps connect.dll IsInternetConnected (section 9: fast-b's for connect).
---
diff --git a/dlls/connect/Makefile.in b/dlls/connect/Makefile.in
--- a/dlls/connect/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/connect/Makefile.in
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 MODULE    = connect.dll
+IMPORTS   = ws2_32 iphlpapi
 
 EXTRADLLFLAGS = -Wb,--prefer-native
 
diff --git a/dlls/connect/main.c b/dlls/connect/main.c
--- a/dlls/connect/main.c
+++ b/dlls/connect/main.c
@@ -21,12 +21,22 @@
 
 #include "windef.h"
 #include "winbase.h"
+#include "winsock2.h"
+#include "ws2ipdef.h"
+#include "iphlpapi.h"
 #include "wine/debug.h"
 
 WINE_DEFAULT_DEBUG_CHANNEL(connect);
 
+/* Connected to the internet when the routing table has an interface for a public address, which needs a
+ * default route: S_OK, otherwise S_FALSE (documented results). */
 HRESULT WINAPI IsInternetConnected(void)
 {
-    FIXME("stub, faking success!\n");
+    SOCKADDR_IN addr = { AF_INET };
+    DWORD index;
+
+    TRACE("\n");
+    addr.sin_addr.s_addr = htonl(0x08080808);  /* 8.8.8.8, any address outside the local networks */
+    if (GetBestInterfaceEx((SOCKADDR *)&addr, &index)) return S_FALSE;
     return S_OK;
 }
